{"name":"Gluon Grey","hex":"#1a1b1c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gluon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A massless gauge boson that binds quarks together to form baryons, mesons and other hadrons and is associated with the strong nuclear force."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gluon"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gluon","blocks":[{"text":"A gluon is a type of massless elementary particle that mediates the strong interaction between quarks, acting as the exchange particle for the interaction. Gluons are massless vector bosons, thereby having a spin of 1. Through the strong interaction, gluons bind quarks into groups according to quantum chromodynamics (QCD), forming hadrons such as protons and neutrons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Feynman_Diagram_Gluon_Radiation.svg/330px-Feynman_Diagram_Gluon_Radiation.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gluon","wikidata":"Q3299"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey","wikidata":"Q42519"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Gluon_tube-color_confinement_animation.gif/50